/ A run saved inside a bound call keeps %!event%: Log is bound before goal Work starts, saves the run there and keeps it
/ in workspace/run.plang. Resumed, the run goes on from the save inside Log and reads %!event!item.name% again: the
/ event that fired, for the goal it fired for. The resumed run goes on through this goal too, from the step after
/ `call Work`: the marker, written after the save, sends it to Resumed, which writes what it saw and ends it.
Start
- before goal Work starts, call Log
- call Work
- if file 'workspace/resumed.marker' exists
    - call Resumed
    - end goal
- write "here" to file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- read file 'workspace/run.plang', write to %snapshot%
- resume %snapshot%
- read file 'workspace/seen.txt', write to %seen%
- assert %seen% equals "Work"
- delete file 'workspace/run.plang'
- delete file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- delete file 'workspace/seen.txt'

/ The goal the event fires for.
Work
- set %worked% = "yes"

/ The bound call: saves the run while it runs, then reads what the event fired for.
Log
- save snapshot, write to %run%
- save %run% to file 'workspace/run.plang'
- set %fired% = %!event!item.name%

/ The resumed run's end: what it saw, written where the asker reads it.
Resumed
- write "%fired%" to file 'workspace/seen.txt'
